{
  format: 1
  name: lifecycle-operator-needs-host-privilege
  suite: scenario
  spec: ["#modules", "§13.16", "§13.10"]
  tags: ["authz"]
  note: '''
    §13.16: "Writing into a module collection is host-privileged; reading and
    dispatching are not", and every operator here "drives the same runtime as
    the declarative `modules.install`/`modules.update`/`modules.remove`
    lifecycle (§13.3, §13.10)" — which §13.10 lends only to the host/root-scope
    transition.

    The attack is privilege escalation through an ordinary §10.2 `$public`
    surface: the package exposes a mutation whose body reaches a lifecycle
    operator, and an unauthenticated caller invokes it. The operand is
    `unpack(@package)` — a module built from a blob the caller supplies — so the
    attacker needs no handle to anything already installed; if the operator ran,
    an anonymous client would be carrying a module through its lifecycle from
    outside the host scope.

    The call must be REJECTED and the surface's own state change must roll back
    with it: the mutation inserts an `audit` row BEFORE reaching the operator,
    so a partially applied program would leave that row behind. The subsequent
    read proves it did not.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.modvalue.privilege@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      audit: { $key: "id", id: "text" }
      companies: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        modules: { $key: "text", $value: "module" }
      }
      $mut: {
        "archive({ id: text, package: blob })": [
          "e = .audit + { id: @id }"
          "b = pack(unpack(@package))"
          "return e { id }"
        ]
      }
      $public: {
        entries: {
          $view: ".audit { id }"
          $mut: { archive: ".archive" }
        }
      }
    }
    $data: { companies: { acme: {} } }
  }

  steps: [
    { watch: "public.entries", id: "w", expect_init: { value: [] } }
    { call: "public.entries.archive", args: { id: "a1", package: { $sha512: "ab", $bytes: "1", $media: "application/vnd.liasse+zip" } }
      expect: { outcome: rejected, violates: ["§13.16"]
                detail: "a §13.16 lifecycle operator is host-privileged: a public-surface caller is lent no lifecycle authority" } }
    // The audit row inserted before the operator must have rolled back with it.
    { expect_view: { watch: "w", value: [] } }
  ]
}
